IMPORT prelude

-- Child Benefit (Rates) Regulations 2006 (S.I. 2006/965) -- LAYER 1, MODULE 1: THE NOUNS.
--
-- Nouns and enumerations only: no rule is defined here and no figure is stated.
-- Every other cbr- module imports this one, so that two chapters of the text cannot
-- each invent their own record for the same person or thing.
--
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2006-965.txt, a plain-text rendering of the CLML of
-- legislation.gov.uk (version 2026-04-06). It is not the official text.
--
-- Layer 1 takes nobody's point of view. A fact that the text leaves to the parent
-- Act (SSCBA / SSCB(NI)A) or to another instrument is a plain field named for the
-- fact, with a comment "-- out of text: ..." as NOTES.md lists.
--
-- REG 1(3) (src:16) governs every field below: a condition satisfied, or a fact
-- existing, is the condition or fact at the BEGINNING OF THE WEEK in question.

§ `Child Benefit (Rates) Regulations 2006 -- nouns and enumerations`

§§ `Regulation 1(2): where a young person is`

-- src:13 | “qualifying young person” means a person—
-- src:14 | (a) in Great Britain, who is such a person for the purposes of Part 9 of SSCBA; and
-- src:15 | (b) in Northern Ireland, who is such a person for the purposes of Part 9 of SSCB(NI)A.
@ref reg 1(2) "qualifying young person" (src:13-15)
DECLARE `Where a young person is` IS ONE OF
    `in Great Britain`
    `in Northern Ireland`
    -- Neither limb (a) nor limb (b) reaches a person elsewhere, so the text makes
    -- no one there a qualifying young person.
    `in neither Great Britain nor Northern Ireland`

§§ `Regulation 2(2): the persons whose circumstances count`

-- src:21 | (2) If, in any week—
-- src:22 | (a) a person is—
-- src:23 | (i) living with his spouse or civil partner,
-- src:24 | (ii) living with another person as his spouse or civil partner, or
-- src:25 | (iii) a member of a polygamous marriage and is residing with other members of that marriage;
-- src:26 | (b) child benefit would, but for this paragraph, be payable to that person in respect of a child or qualifying young person at the enhanced rate; and
-- src:27 | (c) child benefit would, but for this paragraph, be payable at that rate to one of the other persons listed in paragraphs (i) to (iii) of sub-paragraph (a) in respect of another child or qualifying person,
-- src:28 | the enhanced rate shall be payable in that week in respect of only the elder or eldest of the children and qualifying young persons referred to in sub-paragraphs (b) and (c).
@ref reg 2(2) (src:21-28)
DECLARE `Claimant at the start of the week` HAS
    -- reg 2(4)(a): "a voluntary organisation"
    `a voluntary organisation`
        IS A BOOLEAN
    -- reg 2(2)(a)(i): "living with his spouse or civil partner"
    `living with the claimant's spouse or civil partner`
        IS A BOOLEAN
    -- reg 2(2)(a)(ii): "living with another person as his spouse or civil partner"
    `living with another person as the claimant's spouse or civil partner`
        IS A BOOLEAN
    -- reg 2(3)(a): the fact that makes a marriage polygamous
    `during the marriage a party to it is married to more than one person`
        IS A BOOLEAN
    -- reg 2(3)(b): the second fact that makes a marriage polygamous
    `the ceremony of the marriage took place under the law of a country which permits polygamy`
        IS A BOOLEAN
    -- reg 2(2)(a)(iii): "is residing with other members of that marriage"
    `residing with other members of that marriage`
        IS A BOOLEAN

@ref reg 2(2) (src:21-28)
DECLARE `Other persons listed in paragraph (2)(a) at the start of the week` HAS
    -- reg 2(2)(c): whether child benefit would, but for paragraph (2), be payable
    -- at the enhanced rate to ONE OF the other persons for ANOTHER child.
    `child benefit would, but for paragraph (2), be payable at the enhanced rate to one of them for another child or qualifying person`
        IS A BOOLEAN
    -- reg 2(2), closing words: "the elder or eldest of the children and qualifying
    -- young persons referred to in sub-paragraphs (b) and (c)". With several other
    -- persons the elder or eldest of THEIR children is the only one that can matter
    -- to the claimant's child (fork F4); it is read only when the field above is TRUE.
    `date of birth of the elder or eldest of those other children`
        IS A DATE

§§ `Regulation 2(1), (4) and (5): the child and the claim for the child`

-- src:19 | (a) subject to paragraphs (2) to (5), in a case where in any week a child or qualifying young person is the only person or, if not the only person, the elder or eldest person in respect of whom child benefit is payable to a person, £27.05 (“the enhanced rate”);
-- src:20 | (b) in any other case, £17.90.
@ref reg 2(1)(a), (b) (src:19-20)
DECLARE `Case under regulation 2(1)` IS ONE OF
    `the case for the enhanced rate`
    `any other case`

-- src:18 | (1) The weekly rate of child benefit payable in respect of a child or qualifying young person shall be—
-- src:19 | (a) subject to paragraphs (2) to (5), in a case where in any week a child or qualifying young person is the only person or, if not the only person, the elder or eldest person in respect of whom child benefit is payable to a person, £27.05 (“the enhanced rate”);
@ref reg 2(1), (4), (5) (src:18-19)
DECLARE `Child or qualifying young person at the start of the week` HAS
    -- Used only to put two children in order (reg 2(2), closing words): the elder is
    -- the one born earlier.
    `date of birth`
        IS A DATE
    -- Entitlement to child benefit is the parent Act's, not this text's: every rate in
    -- reg 2 is a rate "payable in respect of a child or qualifying young person", so
    -- it is asked as a fact (out of text: SSCBA Part 9 and the Child Benefit (General)
    -- Regulations 2006). Where it is FALSE the text fixes no rate.
    `child benefit is payable to the claimant in respect of the child or qualifying young person`
        IS A BOOLEAN
    -- "child" is not defined in these Regulations: it is the parent Act's word
    -- (out of text: SSCBA Part 9 / SSCB(NI)A Part 9), asked as a fact.
    `a child for the purposes of child benefit`
        IS A BOOLEAN
    -- reg 1(2): the two facts a "qualifying young person" turns on.
    `where the young person is`
        IS A `Where a young person is`
    -- out of text: SSCBA Part 9
    `a qualifying young person for the purposes of Part 9 of SSCBA`
        IS A BOOLEAN
    -- out of text: SSCB(NI)A Part 9
    `a qualifying young person for the purposes of Part 9 of SSCB(NI)A`
        IS A BOOLEAN
    -- reg 2(1)(a), 2(5)(b): "the only person or, if not the only person, the elder or
    -- eldest person in respect of whom child benefit is payable to a person".
    `the only person, or the elder or eldest person, in respect of whom child benefit is payable to the claimant`
        IS A BOOLEAN
    -- reg 2(4)(b): "residing ... with a parent of the child or qualifying young person"
    `the claimant resides with a parent of the child or qualifying young person`
        IS A BOOLEAN
    -- reg 2(4)(b): "(otherwise than as mentioned in paragraph (2)(a))": whether the
    -- claimant lives with that parent as that parent's spouse, civil partner, partner
    -- or fellow member of a polygamous marriage.
    `the claimant resides with that parent as mentioned in paragraph (2)(a)`
        IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Regulation 2(5) and (6): specified benefits`

-- src:39 | (6) The following are specified benefits—
-- src:40 | (a) any benefit under SSCBA receipt of which entitles the recipient to an increase specified in column 2 of the Table in Part 4 of Schedule 4 to that Act (increases for dependants);
-- src:41 | (b) any benefit under SSCB (NI) A receipt of which entitles the recipient to an increase specified in column 2 of the Table in Part IV of Schedule 4 to that Act (increases for dependants in Northern Ireland);
-- src:42 | (c) an allowance for a child or a qualifying young person granted in respect of the death of a person due to service or war injury—
-- src:43 | (i) under the Armed Forces and Reserve Forces (Compensation Scheme) Order 2005;
-- src:44 | (ii) under the Naval, Military and Air Forces Etc. (Disablement and Death) Service Pensions Order 1983;
-- src:45 | (iii) under the Pensions (Polish Forces) Scheme 1964;
-- src:46 | (iv) under the War Pensions (Mercantile Marine) Scheme 1964;
-- src:47 | (v) under the Warrant of 21 st December 1964 concerning pensions and grants in respect of disablement or death due to service in the Home Guard;
-- src:48 | (vi) under the Order of 22 nd December 1964 concerning pensions and grants in respect of disablement or death due to service in the Home Guard after 27 th April 1952;
-- src:49 | (vii) under the Order by Her Majesty dated 4 th January 1971 in respect of service in the Ulster Defence Regiment; or
-- src:50 | (viii) which the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs accept as being analogous to an allowance for a child granted in respect of the death of a person due to service or war injury under any of the preceding provisions of this sub-paragraph.
@ref reg 2(6) (src:39-50)
DECLARE `Kind of payment made for the week` IS ONE OF
    `a benefit under SSCBA`
    `a benefit under SSCB(NI)A`
    `an allowance for a child or a qualifying young person granted in respect of the death of a person due to service or war injury`
    `a payment of some other kind`

@ref reg 2(6)(c) (src:39-50)
DECLARE `Instrument granting an allowance for a child on a death due to service or war injury` IS ONE OF
    `the Armed Forces and Reserve Forces (Compensation Scheme) Order 2005`
    `the Naval, Military and Air Forces Etc. (Disablement and Death) Service Pensions Order 1983`
    `the Pensions (Polish Forces) Scheme 1964`
    `the War Pensions (Mercantile Marine) Scheme 1964`
    `the Warrant of 21st December 1964 concerning pensions and grants in respect of disablement or death due to service in the Home Guard`
    `the Order of 22nd December 1964 concerning pensions and grants in respect of disablement or death due to service in the Home Guard after 27th April 1952`
    `the Order by Her Majesty dated 4th January 1971 in respect of service in the Ulster Defence Regiment`
    `an instrument not listed in paragraph (6)(c)(i) to (vii)`

@ref reg 2(5), (6) (src:39-50)
DECLARE `Payment made for the week` HAS
    `kind of payment`
        IS A `Kind of payment made for the week`
    -- reg 2(6)(a), (b): "receipt of which entitles the recipient to an increase
    -- specified in column 2 of the Table in Part 4 of Schedule 4 to that Act".
    -- out of text: SSCBA Schedule 4 Part 4; SSCB(NI)A Schedule 4 Part IV.
    `receipt of the benefit entitles the recipient to an increase for dependants specified in the Table in Schedule 4 to that Act`
        IS A BOOLEAN
    `instrument granting the allowance`
        IS A `Instrument granting an allowance for a child on a death due to service or war injury`
    -- reg 2(6)(c)(viii): a judgment the text hands to the Commissioners for Her
    -- Majesty's Revenue and Customs, taken as a conditional input.
    `the Commissioners accept the allowance as analogous to one granted under those instruments`
        IS A BOOLEAN
    -- reg 2(5)(a): "is paid in respect of a week ... to a person"
    `paid to the claimant in respect of the week`
        IS A BOOLEAN
    -- reg 2(5)(b): "in respect of the only, elder or eldest child"
    `paid in respect of the child or qualifying young person`
        IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Regulation 3: the saving`

-- src:56 | (2) In paragraph (1) “the relevant transitional provisions and savings” means—
-- src:57 | (a) in the case of child benefit payable under SSCBA, regulations 3 and 4 of the Child Benefit and Social Security (Fixing and Adjustment of Rates) (Amendment) Regulations 1998 ; and
-- src:58 | (b) in the case of child benefit payable under SSCB(NI)A, regulations 3 and 4 of the Child Benefit and Social Security (Fixing and Adjustment of Rates) (Amendment) Regulations (Northern Ireland) 1998 .
@ref reg 3(2) (src:56-58)
DECLARE `Act under which child benefit is payable` IS ONE OF
    `child benefit payable under SSCBA`
    `child benefit payable under SSCB(NI)A`

@ref reg 3(2) (src:56-58)
DECLARE `Transitional provisions and savings in regulation 3(2)` IS ONE OF
    `regulations 3 and 4 of the Child Benefit and Social Security (Fixing and Adjustment of Rates) (Amendment) Regulations 1998`
    `regulations 3 and 4 of the Child Benefit and Social Security (Fixing and Adjustment of Rates) (Amendment) Regulations (Northern Ireland) 1998`

§§ `Regulation 4: the Table of revocations`

-- src:59 | 4 Revocations
-- src:60 | The provisions listed in column 1 of the Table are, to the extent shown in column 2, revoked.
@ref reg 4 (src:59-60)
DECLARE `Extent of a revocation under regulation 4` IS ONE OF
    `the whole instrument`
    -- Column 2 names the provisions revoked, in the text's own words ("Regulation 2.").
    `part of the instrument` HAS `provisions revoked` IS A STRING

@ref reg 4 (src:59-60)
DECLARE `Row of the Table in regulation 4` HAS
    `row`                  IS A NUMBER
    -- Column 1, without the footnote number the converter fused to it.
    `instrument`           IS A STRING
    -- The footnote to column 1, without its number.
    `citation`             IS A STRING
    `extent of revocation` IS A `Extent of a revocation under regulation 4`
